/**
 * Self-signed fixture certificates for keychain team detection tests, shaped
 * like Apple Development identities: the subject carries UID, CN (with the
 * Apple ID email), OU (the team id), O and C. Generated once with OpenSSL 3
 * and embedded so the tests never touch a real keychain or shell out:
 *
 *   openssl req -x509 -newkey ec -pkeyopt ec_paramgen_curve:prime256v1 \
 *     -nodes -keyout /dev/null -out cert.pem \
 *     -subj "/UID=UID<team>/CN=Apple Development: <email> (<keyid>)/OU=<team>/O=Fixture Dev/C=US" \
 *     -not_before <YYYYMMDDHHMMSSZ> -not_after 20990101000000Z
 *
 * The throwaway keys were never written anywhere; the certificates certify
 * nothing and exist only to be parsed.
 */

